  ! The template variable title hides a variable with the same name.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <div v-for="title in 5"></div>
      │               ^^^^^
    4 │   <div v-for="item in 5"></div>
    5 │ </template>
  
  i The hidden title is declared here.
  
     7 │ <script setup lang="ts">
   > 8 │ defineProps<{ title: string }>();
       │               ^^^^^
     9 │ const item = "selected";
    10 │ </script>
  
  i Inside this element, title refers to the template variable, so the other title can't be used, and the two are easy to confuse.
  
  i Rename the template variable.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

